[33m▲[39m  Storybook found TypeScript 7.0.2 as the `typescript` package.
[90m│[39m  TypeScript 7 does not include the compiler API that Storybook uses to
[90m│[39m  read your component types for Controls and the Docs args table.

[90m│[39m  If package.json has no `typescript` entry, your package manager
[90m│[39m  installed TypeScript 7 for Storybook's peer dependency. Add
[90m│[39m  `typescript@^6` to the devDependencies in package.json.

[90m│[39m  If your project uses TypeScript 7, install TypeScript 7 and TypeScript
[90m│[39m  6 side by side. In package.json, replace the `typescript` entry in
[90m│[39m  devDependencies with these two entries:

[90m│[39m  "@typescript/native": "npm:typescript@^7.0.2",
[90m│[39m  "typescript": "npm:@typescript/typescript6@^6.0.2"

[90m│[39m  `tsc` stays on TypeScript 7, and the `typescript` package is
[90m│[39m  TypeScript 6. Both entries are necessary.

[90m│[39m  Then install dependencies and restart Storybook.

[90m│[39m  Until then, Storybook falls back to the deprecated builder docgen with
[90m│[39m  `react-docgen`, which will be removed in Storybook 12.

